# Copy to .env.local and fill in to turn on household sharing.
# Without these, CartWise runs entirely on the device and the sign-in UI is
# hidden — no dead buttons, no network calls.
#
# Both values come from your Supabase project: Settings -> API.
#
# The anon key is designed to be public. It identifies the project, and every
# table is protected by row-level security (see supabase/schema.sql). It is
# safe in the bundle.
#
# The service_role key is the secret one. It bypasses row-level security
# entirely. Never put it in this file, in the client, or in the repo.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
